{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"fdc0e13729996699","type":"text","text":"[https://chatgpt.com/share/697071ff-9a9c-8005-ace2-da1d215f8adb](https://chatgpt.com/share/697071ff-9a9c-8005-ace2-da1d215f8adb \"https://chatgpt.com/share/697071ff-9a9c-8005-ace2-da1d215f8adb\") -> brainstorming\n","x":-282,"y":-266,"width":682,"height":50},
		{"id":"616798ae637953b7","type":"text","text":"1. Semantic data set (anchor)\n\t1. center of everything\n\t2. it says\n\t\t1. what this data is?\n\t\t2. at what granularity?\n\t\t3. is it observed or predicted?\n\t\t4. what modality is it?\n\t3. This became your system of semantic truth\n2. semantic fields\n\t1. This defines column level meaning\n\t\t1. Metric vs dimension\n\t\t2. regrettable or not\n\t\t3. business names, synonyms, examples\n\t\t4. Embeddings\n\t2. This prevents\n\t\t1. wrong aggregations\n\t\t2. misuse in BI\n\t\t3. LLM hallucinations\n3. Processing metadata\n\t1. Instead of separate batch and stream tables, you unified them.\n\t2. This allows:\n\t\t1. “Is this real-time or historical?”\n\t\t2. “How fresh is this data?”\n\t3. Without branching logic.\n4. SLA and quality\n\t1. You added **trust signals**:\n\t\t1. Latency\n\t\t2. Freshness\n\t\t3. Availability\n\t\t4. Expected volume\n\t2. This allows both humans and machines to judge **reliability**.\n5. Asset Technical Metadata\n\t1. One generic table handles:\n\t\t1. Video, Audio, Image, Text\n\t2. Instead of one table per modality.\n\t3. This keeps the model scalable and simple.\n6. Semantic enrichment and AI outputs\n\t1. LLMs should query AI outputs and enrichments, not raw media\n7. ML outputs\n\t1. you separated predicted data and observed data. \n\t2. so llm can answer safely:\n\t\t1. this is a forecast not fact.\n8. Dataset relationships (lineage)\n\t1. you captured \n\t\t1. derives from\n\t\t2. enriches\n\t\t3. aggregates\n\t\t4. trains\n\t2. this works as \n\t\t1. relational joins\n\t\t2. graph ","x":-221,"y":-180,"width":560,"height":1380},
		{"id":"31c55fd4ce3911fb","type":"text","text":"#### Step 1: Pick a Sample Domain","x":-106,"y":-4360,"width":330,"height":87},
		{"id":"8cd521d95dc37e25","type":"text","text":"Customer Support domain:\n\nSample Data Assets\n- Customer support calls (audio)\n- Call transcripts (text)\n- Call sentiment scores (ML output)\n\nThis gives us:\n- Unstructured data \n- AI enrichment\n- Observed vs predicted semantics","x":504,"y":-4480,"width":362,"height":327},
		{"id":"5ef40ae67eb19479","type":"text","text":"#### Step 2:  Add Processing Meaning (Batch vs Stream)","x":-111,"y":-4196,"width":340,"height":86},
		{"id":"8803f106d287fead","type":"text","text":"Question for this step/ we want metadata to answer:\n- “Is this real-time or historical?”\n\n```json\n{\n  \"dataset_id\": \"cust_support_calls\",\n  \"processing\": {\n    \"type\": \"batch\",\n    \"load\": \"incremental\",\n    \"frequency\": \"hourly\",\n    \"retention_hours\": 720,\n    \"late_arrival_policy\": \"accept\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Plain meaning\n\n- This data is **not real-time**\n- It updates **hourly**\n- We keep it for **30 days**\nNo system needed this is **meaning captured**.","x":-1056,"y":-4441,"width":520,"height":576},
		{"id":"5ef412cdc983f8d5","type":"text","text":"#### Step 3: Add AI meaning ( sematic enrichment)\n","x":-106,"y":-3993,"width":330,"height":80},
		{"id":"a5f30e55e65f2a77","type":"text","text":"Question we want metadata to answer\n- “What meaning can we extract from this data?”\n\n```json\n{\n  \"dataset_id\": \"cust_support_calls\",\n  \"semantic_enrichment\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"transcription\",\n      \"model\": \"whisper\",\n      \"version\": \"v3\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.93,\n      \"output\": \"Call transcript available\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nPlain meaning\n- This audio has **text meaning**\n- Generated by AI\n- With **93% confidence**\nLLMs read this  **not the audio**.\n\n","x":904,"y":-4223,"width":447,"height":540},
		{"id":"6c6a81d19a6aac13","type":"text","text":"#### Step 4: separate fact from prediction","x":-106,"y":-3820,"width":330,"height":80},
		{"id":"6f3d397a4b788bd4","type":"text","text":"#### Step 5: Add relationships\n","x":-106,"y":-3660,"width":330,"height":80},
		{"id":"db28fd860516a18d","type":"text","text":"#### Step 6: Add trust rules ","x":-106,"y":-3520,"width":330,"height":80},
		{"id":"ca804b3ff9355528","type":"text","text":"#### Step 7: Add trust summary","x":-106,"y":-3360,"width":330,"height":80},
		{"id":"c9266fe4867bf867","type":"text","text":"https://chatgpt.com/share/6970d0ad-1888-8005-a3f1-99e5609a0651 -> chats ","x":-362,"y":-4640,"width":843,"height":83},
		{"id":"00e359ab9bfd58e0","x":-280,"y":-2860,"width":450,"height":155,"type":"text","text":"> **Tables and columns describe _how data is stored_.  \n> Unified metadata describes _what data means_.  \n> Visualization should always follow meaning, not storage.**\n\n"}
	],
